WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.569
-This is very exciting. You
started doing stand-up again.

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:05.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
You filmed a Netflix special
that's coming? Yes?

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.273 line:92%
And what has it been like

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.309 size:81% position:41%
being back on the road
doing stand-up again?

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.677
Because I know you took a break
for a while.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I hadn't done stand-up
in 10 years.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:16.916
And I'd done it for 15 years
prior to the first "Hangover."

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.320 size:84% position:42%
So that's how I really
got my start in comedy.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.821 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it has been amazing.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's been basically

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
very personal,
very autobiographical,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's really like a one-man
show with [bleep] jokes.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know? It's just so --
Small [bleep] jokes.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.402 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And --

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.773 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It's, like, very short.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.908 line:92%
-Very short. Yeah. Very short.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a setup and
a punch line, and we get out.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:48.548 size:78% position:39%
-And some may call it
unsatisfying. Now...

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
But it's very nice.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:53.453 line:92%
You really kind of get to see --

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:56.356
The first movie I did
was Judd Apatow's "Knocked Up."

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:59.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I shot that movie
while still having my day job.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.527 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And really therapeutic

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
to kind of go over
the last 10 years of my life.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my wife's
a breast-cancer survivor.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:06.699 line:92%
She's 10 years cancer-free.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:14.340 size:78% position:39%
And it's really nice.
I had forgotten --

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.843 size:81% position:41%
Before "The Hangover"
became "The Hangover,"

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had actually turned down
the part of Mr. Chow.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.147 line:92%
And there's a whole backstory

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
of how I eventually
did the part.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's lovely.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:27.854
-And because of what your wife
was going through at the time,

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
while you were shooting
"The Hangover,"

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.324
it was a difficult time for you,
which I'm assuming

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.759 line:92%
people would think was this

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
transcendentally great time
for you.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.296 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah. It was cathartic.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.530 size:84% position:42% line:92%
In fact, I did in-jokes

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
because Tran was going
through chemo at that time.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:43.703
And I did in-jokes in Vietnamese
that made it in the movie

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.972 line:92%
just to make my wife laugh.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.407 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
When Mr. Chow...

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.042 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cackles as Mr. Chow ]

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
When Mr. Chow
is releasing Black Doug,

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.481 line:92%
he says [Speaks Vietnamese]

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it doesn't mean "release
the hostage" in Chinese.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.785 size:88% position:44%
Actually, in Vietnamese,
it means "chicken die."

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
For some reason,
that just came up.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so a lot of these
Vietnamese words

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.190 line:92%
are sprinkled in the final cut.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you put as much thought
into Mr. Chow's backstory

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
as those people did
for their Santa Claus?

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.433 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I didn't choose Chow.

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Mr. Chow ]
Chow chose me!

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:19.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] I believe that.
I believe that.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have another show
that's coming up.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called -- What --
-It's "The Masked Singer."

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"The Masked Singer."
-Yeah.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Explain how the show works
real quick.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's based on
basically the most popular

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
competition show
in Korea and Thailand.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:42.595
I'm Korean, and this is my mom's
favorite show in Korea.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.431 size:84% position:42%
And I got offered to be
a judge on this show,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.600 line:92%
and I was going to turn it down.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.668 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I wasn't sure about it.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my mom's like,
"You have to do this show!"

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like,
"You don't understand, Mom.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.941
I have no -- what's the word --
talent.

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know anything
about music."

00:02:58.645 --> 00:02:59.646 size:75% position:38% line:92%
She was just like --

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
She sent me YouTube clips
in Korean,

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:04.450 line:92%
like, tapes of the Korean show.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.319 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's so oddly perfect.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.722
It's so amazing, where you're --
It's part like "The Voice."

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like the blind auditions
in "The Voice."

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:13.793 line:92%
It's part "American Idol."

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's part, like,
"This Is Your Life."

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.664
It's four different competitions
rolled into one.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the part
that you've left out

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is maybe
the most jarringly different

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
is "The Masked Singer"
is someone we know,

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:26.973
but once they reveal themselves,
we'll know who they are.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.840 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They're famous.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everyone's recognizable.
Everyone's famous.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:34.647
At the end of every episode
when contestants are eliminated,

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.316 line:92%
when you hear their testimonials

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:39.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
of why they chose to do this
in the first place,

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.353 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it's oddly emotional.

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:43.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were a couple times
I teared up, like, literally.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:47.827
"Oh, my God. I love you, Hippo!"
Or whatever. I don't know.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.229 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's the thing.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.331
When you think of masked singer,
you think of just a mask.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:54.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that's a lot more
than just a mask.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this is would be
a celebrity singing.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It is. It is.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.406 line:92%
-And then they give you clues,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have to guess
who they are.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:06.179
No one at home right now is
thinking, "Oh, I had that idea."

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
It's amazing, though.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at the layer of it,
you know?

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:14.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a bunny,
but it's Donnie Darko.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's got some
spookiness to it.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We look forward to that,
as well.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always just so great
to see you, man.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for being here.
Really appreciate it.

